    "notes": "Read all seven current steps and direct supplier clauses. Quadratic contraction is symmetric, trace vanishes in dimension four and polynomial C1 components meet tensor regularity. Checked T00=u, T0i=S_i/c=cg_i, Tij=-sigma_ij, including zero fields and SI units. Contracting the cyclic identity gives C_nu=partial_nu(F\u00b2)/4, canceling the quadratic derivative and leaving divergence -F^{nu lambda}j_lambda. Component signs match local Poynting/momentum balance; only local clauses (a), not their Countable-Choice integral branches, are used. Matter tensor is independently assumed C1 symmetric with opposite divergence; finite-box Riemann theorem retains side fluxes and requires vanishing sides for slice constancy. Angular divergence vanishes by symmetry. Weak/distribution products excluded. No global/infinite-volume conservation, empirical premise or choice. Beisert locator p9.10 (9.51)-(9.53) verified in primary PDF; source-only correction retained."
